comments[11]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-11T13:53:41.933Z","harness:claude-code","Adoption baseline measured 2026-08-11, immediately after the assurance primitives shipped in 2026.8.11.\n\nThe capability is complete. pm-2lex4r (measure), pm-lyfu7b (assert), pm-wn6wot (gate) and pm-91xeam (verdicts) are all closed, pm assurance exposes list, show, put, remove, run and verdicts, and docs/ASSURANCE.md documents nine measurement sources, seven assertion polarities, three scopes, two lifetimes and three enforcement levels.\n\nNothing uses it.\n\n- pm assurance list measurement, list assertion and list gate all return count 0.\n- .agents/pm/assurance.json does not exist.\n- grep for assurance across .github/workflows/ and scripts/ returns one incidental hit in a token baseline JSON file and no invocation.\n\nMeanwhile the enforcement the project actually relies on is still declared elsewhere: scripts/release/tracker-measurements.json holds 30 declarations across five selector sources (health_check 10, dependency_kind 6, graph_finding 5, graph_profile 4, validate_warning 5), and the only reader is scripts/release/tracker-measurement-gate.mjs.\n\nSo the project now has two enforcement vocabularies. The one that ships inside the product has zero members and zero consumers. The one that gates every release lives in a script this item exists to retire. That is the same producer-and-consumer asymmetry recorded as roadmap horizon AG, applied to the mechanism that was built to end it.\n\nThis is the starting state for the per-script disposition this item owns, and it is also why the disposition should be written as declarations rather than as prose: every row of tracker-measurements.json that has an equivalent assurance source can be expressed today, and each one that cannot names a genuine provider gap for pm-uhv1m5.\n"
  "2026-08-12T14:33:40.398Z","harness:codex","Orientation evidence: live repository already dogfoods two native assurance gates at current head, superseding the older no-use snapshot in this item comment history. This tranche will inventory every bespoke release gate, migrate coherent local checks to native assurance/provider primitives, and retain only gates whose orchestration cannot be represented honestly."
  "2026-08-12T14:58:23.386Z","harness:codex","Scope decision from implementation evidence: this tranche supplies the missing extension-provider and preset primitives, but the migration item cannot honestly close without deleting/reducing bespoke scripts, proving each replacement negative control, reducing external gate LOC, and reaching a migrated majority. A prose-only ledger would not satisfy those live acceptance criteria. No migration-source edit was made; returning this item to open/unclaimed so only actively implemented work remains in progress. The provider work in pm-uhv1m5 is the explicit prerequisite for later coverage/eval/registry/service script reductions."
  "2026-08-12T22:09:11.705Z","harness:codex","Start evidence 2026-08-13: selected after live all-status orientation (2453 items, zero pre-existing in-progress), full assurance lineage review, and GitHub/security/dependency inventory. This branch will remove the legacy tracker-measurement script/config in favor of SDK-evaluated declarations, add a machine-checked disposition for every gate script, and keep retained external-orchestration gates honest."
  "2026-08-12T23:27:46.923Z","harness:codex","Tranche evidence: tracker-measurement-gate.mjs, its declaration JSON, and 1,140 lines of bespoke tests are removed and replaced by 30+ SDK-native measurements, 38 assertions, cached graph/validate/health snapshots, and CI/release package invocations. The fail-closed inventory covers every current gate script and every graph operation; the linked suites pass 79/79, the full repository passes 7,236 tests at exact 100/100/100/100, and installed npm/npx plus Bun/bunx CLI and SDK acceptance passes. This item remains open because the live ledger is 1 migrated versus 14 retained: the acceptance criterion requiring a migrated majority is deliberately not claimed by this tranche."
  "2026-08-12T23:57:36.694Z","harness:codex","Final tranche evidence after recursive correction: the native tracker gate contains 37 passing assertions and replaces the 929-line tracker-measurement gate, 327-line bespoke declaration file, and 1,140-line bespoke test suite. The machine ledger exactly covers every gate script and graph operation; exact coverage, static quality, package artifact, npx smoke, and package-first dogfood pass. The item remains open because the honest ledger is still 1 migrated versus 14 retained, so the migrated-majority acceptance criterion is not met."
  "2026-08-13T00:01:39.635Z","harness:codex","Implementation PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/992 — first native gate migration and exhaustive automation disposition ledger; item remains open for migrated-majority follow-up."
  "2026-08-13T01:01:49.563Z","harness:codex","Review-fix evidence: release gate discovery now includes JS/TS ESM/CJS variants, inventories static-quality-gate.mts, and consumes the built SDK GRAPH_SUBCOMMAND_VALUES contract instead of copying 16 operations. Static quality passes with zero inventory violations, 100% docstrings, and no complexity or boundary regressions."
  "2026-08-13T01:08:52.039Z","harness:codex","Final local evidence: quality:static passes the complete native assurance and fail-closed automation inventory; package artifact gate passes; full suite and exact coverage pass. PR review responses now map each accepted or declined finding to its concrete implementation/rationale."
  "2026-08-13T02:44:19.425Z","harness:codex","CI diagnosis: exact head 93c5f5b48 failed only the native tracker-context-quality gate because a clean hosted runner generated one advisory telemetry health warning during preceding CLI invocations. SDK health explicitly treats telemetry warnings as advisory; the new assurance declaration incorrectly enforced health-telemetry-zero as blocking. Correcting the declaration and adding focused policy evidence before rerunning exact-head CI."
  "2026-08-13T02:51:39.935Z","harness:codex","TDD/CI repair evidence: the focused policy test failed first against blocking health-telemetry-zero, then passed after enforcement became warn with authorization_decision pm-jezo. pnpm quality:static now passes the full native tracker/graph/record assurance sequence on the same local repository state that carries queued telemetry warnings; ESLint and history validation also pass. The broader migration remains open because its migrated-majority criterion is not yet met."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-12T23:27:47.477Z","harness:codex","A native gate migration needs two inventories: executable dispositions prove no bespoke script vanished silently, while operation consumers prove shipped analytical primitives are either automated or deliberately interactive. The product must also cache provider snapshots per gate context or a wide declaration set multiplies expensive scans."
